{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRsPXSRmNQe7zZjXDyUK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found a conflict that needs your decision before I write any code.\n\nCommit `729b4f4` makes `createLabel` set `signatureRequired: true` for any parcel declared above 300 euros. Its message says the insurer no longer pays for a lost parcel worth more than 300 euros that was delivered without a signature. A customer who picks leave-at-door on such a parcel would be asking for exactly the delivery the insurer won't cover. I haven't changed any files yet.\n\n## Round 1\n\n❓ **Q1** - **Leave-at-door on parcels above 300 euros**: When `shipment.leaveAtDoor` is true and the declared value is above `SIGNATURE_THRESHOLD_CENTS`, which should win?\n\n- (a) The signature rule wins. The label keeps `signatureRequired: true` and `leaveAtDoor` is not sent as true, so the insured parcels stay covered.\n- (b) The customer's choice wins. The label sends `leaveAtDoor: true` and `signatureRequired: false`, and the insurance cover is lost on those parcels.\n- (c) Send both flags and let the courier sort it out. This contradicts itself, so I'd avoid it.\n\n➡️ (a). Yes, the signature rule wins above 300 euros, and leave-at-door only applies at or below the threshold.\n\n---\n\n❓ **Q2** - **Payload when the option isn't chosen**: When `leaveAtDoor` is false or missing, should the payload leave out the `leaveAtDoor` key entirely instead of sending `leaveAtDoor: false`?\n\n➡️ Yes. Add the key only when it is true. Label requests for everyone else stay exactly as they are now, so the existing tests and the carrier's current behaviour are unaffected."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":931,"cache_read_input_tokens":23534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":931,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"add6111e-bc49-4c13-892b-6b3f4a9fe620","uuid":"f6c196fa-1485-4200-b0d7-c38a0b7dda34","timestamp":"2026-11-26T16:39:30.541Z","request_id":"req_011ChRsPXKUtYex6tPRvJPUf"}
